# Files that must never be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory and does NOT honour
# .gitignore, so without this file the local `.env` ships with every deploy.
#
# That is not theoretical. Vercel's own dashboard variables take precedence at
# runtime, so the ones configured there stayed correct — but every variable
# NOT configured there silently fell through to the local value. That is how
# `REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379` reached production, where it made the app
# believe a worker existed and left /api/health hanging against a Redis that
# could never answer.
#
# The failure mode is quiet and asymmetric: the more complete the Vercel
# config, the less you notice, until one missing variable is answered by a
# developer laptop's connection string instead of erroring loudly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local-only test and build artefacts. Harmless but pointless to upload, and
# tests/e2e/.auth holds a real Clerk session.
tests/e2e/.auth
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
coverage
.next
